FOUNDING EDICTS OF THE FIRST HOKAGE
Hashirama Senju, Shodai Hokage — Archive Transcript

Upon the founding of Konohagakure through the accord between the
Senju and Uchiha clans, the First Hokage set down these principles:

1. The village exists so that children need not die on battlefields
   as our generation did. The Will of Fire binds all who dwell here.
2. Clans shall lay down old feuds within the village walls. The
   Uchiha, Senju, and all founding clans are equal under the leaf.
3. The tailed beasts held by this village are a trust, not a weapon
   of first resort. (Note: appended distribution of beasts to other
   villages was made to preserve the fragile peace.)
4. The Hokage serves the village; the village does not serve the
   Hokage.

Hashirama Senju is remembered as the God of Shinobi, wielder of the
Wood Release. His edicts remain the foundation of village law. See
the founding charter for the full constitutional text.
